Interview care points

1) Redis is great as **cache / speed layer**, not always as sole source of truth for critical durable business data (unless designed carefully with persistence + HA).
2) Eviction: when memory full, policies like LRU/LFU can drop keys — fine for cache, dangerous if you assumed durability.
3) Persistence: RDB (snapshots), AOF (append log) — tradeoffs speed vs durability.
4) Client in Spring: typically **Lettuce** (default) or Jedis.

